{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:12403254 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:12403254 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":1,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"12403254","source":"MED","pmid":"12403254","title":"Prevention of antibiotic-associated diarrhea in infants by probiotics.","authorString":"Jirapinyo P, Densupsoontorn N, Thamonsiri N, Wongarn R.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Jirapinyo P","firstName":"Pipop","lastName":"Jirapinyo","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Pediatrics, Faculty of Medicine Siriraj Hospital, Mahidol University, Bangkok, Thailand."}]}},{"fullName":"Densupsoontorn N","firstName":"Narumon","lastName":"Densupsoontorn","initials":"N"},{"fullName":"Thamonsiri N","firstName":"Nuchnoi","lastName":"Thamonsiri","initials":"N"},{"fullName":"Wongarn R","firstName":"Renu","lastName":"Wongarn","initials":"R"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"85 Suppl 2","journalIssueId":1129011,"dateOfPublication":"2002 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2002,"printPublicationDate":"2002-08-01","journal":{"title":"Journal of the Medical Association of Thailand = Chotmaihet thangphaet","medlineAbbreviation":"J Med Assoc Thai","essn":"2408-1981","issn":"0125-2208","isoabbreviation":"J Med Assoc Thai","nlmid":"7507216"}},"pubYear":"2002","pageInfo":"S739-42","abstractText":"Probiotics administration has been claimed to prevent antibiotic-associated diarrhea. The investigators thus conducted a double blind, placebo controlled study of providing probiotics to infants and children with severe bacterial infections and receiving broad spechum antibiotics. The results of the study showed that the group receiving probiotics had fewer diarrheal episodes (37.5%) than the control group (80%), although the numbers were too small for statistical analysis. In conclusion, probiotics administration to patients receiving high doses of broad spectrum antibiotics may prevent the occurrence of antibiotic-associated diarrhea. A further study with a larger number is required.","affiliation":"Department of Pediatrics, Faculty of Medicine Siriraj Hospital, Mahidol University, Bangkok, Thailand.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Comparative Study","Clinical Trial","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Lactobacillus acidophilus"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Bacteremia","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Meningitis, Bacterial","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Diarrhea","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"CI","qualifierName":"chemically induced","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"PC","qualifierName":"prevention & control","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Anti-Bacterial Agents","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"AD","qualifierName":"administration & dosage","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Treatment Outcome"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Administration, Oral"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Follow-Up Studies"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Double-Blind Method"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Dose-Response Relationship, Drug"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Reference Values"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Probiotics","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"AD","qualifierName":"ad